Meriem Bennani never set out to make a movie quite as personal as &#x201C; Bouchra .&#x201D;

&#x201C;I'm a pretty private person &#x2014; hard to believe, probably, after seeing this film,&#x201D; Bennani joked, sitting with her co-director Orian Barki for a Variety&#x2019;s Screening Series Q&A.

Sure, the animated film was always a work of autofiction: &#x201C;Bouchra&#x201D; explores the journey of a 35-year-old Moroccan lesbian navigating life and love in New York City and writing the script for an autobiographical film. (Bouchra, the title character, is a jackal and all the cast are anthropomorphic animals, mirroring the duo&#x2019;s first project, the 2020 web series &#x201C;2 Lizards.&#x201D;) The movie was also inspired by Bennani's mother&#x2019;s reaction to her coming out as queer. But the movie wasn&#x2019;t supposed to be about their relationship. So how did it end up that way? blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Hold Onto Me' Director Myrsini Aristidou Kicks Off Historic Oscar Campaign for Sundance Audience Award Winner: 'I Really Feel Like We're Underdogs'

Bennani and Barki had begun developing the project with their collaborators, cinematographer John Michael Boling and head of animation Jason Coombs, but something wasn&#x2019;t quite clicking.

&#x201C;We had the script, but as we were editing the dialogues and starting to put the storyboards [together], we felt like there was something we were still looking for, and it&#x2019;s the heart of the film," Bennani recalled.

So, she told Barki she needed to call her mom to get more insight into her perspective. Why did she react that way when Bennani came out? The call was purely for research, but Bennani knew it&#x2019;d be prudent to record the conversation.

&#x201C;I knew I would be too emotional to be there as a director. I would be there as a daughter,&#x201D; she explained. &#x201C;So I recorded them and then I played them for Orian. &#x2026; And we knew in that moment, that was the film and that we needed to put these conversations in the film.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Those recordings became the new framework for the movie as the filmmakers lasered in on this personal narrative over a more synthesized version of a Moroccan lesbian's experience.

&#x201C;Through specificity, you can reach truth,&#x201D; Bennani said. &#x201C;And when I say truth, I don&#x2019;t mean realism. Just an emotional truth.&#x201D;

The experimental indie film debuted as part of Bennani&#x2019;s art exhibition at Fondazione Prada in Milan (which backed the film), then was part of the official selection at TIFF in 2025. The feature has picked up a handful of prizes as it traveled the art house and film festival circuits, including the Gold Q-Hugo prize at the Chicago International Film Festival. (&#x201C;Bouchra&#x201D; is now streaming on Mubi.)

&#x201C;People are really into seeing a film that is original and looks different and is so handcrafted,&#x201D; Barki said, reflecting on the positive response. &#x201C;I was happy to see that people are just down for a new story and a new visual.&#x201D;

One of the most poignant pieces of feedback came from a friend who told Barki, &#x201C;I always thought that my parents loving me means that they have to understand everything about me. And maturing, I learned that I can receive their love without them having to actually understand every detail of my existence the same way that I understand it.&#x201D;

Without necessarily intending to, Barki&#x2019;s friend had zeroed in on a central theme of the meta movie.

&#x201C;The movie is about a mother-daughter relationship that has this foundation of love, [which] is what gets them to have all these conversations,&#x201D; Barki explained. &#x201C;And in a way, it doesn't matter if they'll understand everything about it, but just the willingness to have this conversation is already the acceptance and the love.&#x201D;

Watch the video above to learn more about Bennani and Barki&#x2019;s artistry; how they drew inspiration from Wong Kar-wai&#x2019;s &#x201C;Chungking Express&#x201D; and Martin Scorsese&#x2019;s &#x201C;After Hours&#x201D;; and what Bennani&#x2019;s mother made of the finished film.

EXCLUSIVE : Tony-winning Ivy Lion Productions has secured development capital for IP acquisitions and recently switched management from Zero Gravity to the Gotham Group .

Last season, at the age of 33, Ivy Lion's Lamar Richardson became the youngest Black lead producer to win a Tony (Best Revival of Musical for Ragtime ).

