Mckenna Grace has been on a red carpet run for the ages during the global press tour for &#x201C;The Hunger Games : Sunrise on the Reaping.&#x201D;

Over the last few weeks, the 20-year-old actress (and certified &#x201C;Hunger Games&#x201D; fangirl) has donned nearly two dozen looks that referenced the original trilogy or franchise star Jennifer Lawrence. Grace, who plays District 12 tribute Maysilee Donner (and her twin sister, Merilee), launched the tour with an archival Monique Lhuillier gown that evoked Lawrence's wedding dress as Katniss in &#x201C;Catching Fire.&#x201D; Then, for the film&#x2019;s final premiere on Monday night in New York City, Grace glided onto the red carpet in a cobalt blue Pamella Roland gown &#x2014; with feathered wings! &#x2014; mirroring the iconic Mockingjay look that bridal gown turned into. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Hold Onto Me' Director Myrsini Aristidou Kicks Off Historic Oscar Campaign for Sundance Audience Award Winner: 'I Really Feel Like We're Underdogs'

Like Katniss, Grace&#x2019;s Maysilee aims to defy the Capitol &#x2014; something the actress wanted to portray in real life, too.

&#x201C;Maysilee&#x2019;s form of rebellion was also her style and holding onto her personality in the face of the Capitol,&#x201D; Grace told Variety's Antonio Ferme at the New York City premiere. &#x201C;I felt like I&#x2019;d be doing myself a disservice not paying homage to all of the incredible performers and costume designers from the previous films.&#x201D;

Grace joined Variety for a longer chat a few days earlier, checking in on Zoom the morning after the Los Angeles fan event for &#x201C;Sunrise on the Reaping,&#x201D; where she recreated another of Katniss&#x2019; dresses from &#x201C;Catching Fire.&#x201D; With just two stops left on the press tour (Mexico and New York City), Grace is in between fittings for her final two outfits, both of which paid homage to the mockingjay that started it all. After all, her character is the original owner of the mockingjay pin. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Her character, Maysilee, is the hot-headed, dignified ally of Haymitch Abernathy (Joseph Zada), who similarly wishes to take down the Capitol and stop the Hunger Games. Although District 12 is known as the poorest district, she prides herself in her fine dresses and overzealous amounts of jewelry &#x2014; something she continues to prioritize after being reaped.

&#x201C;I didn't want it to be like, &#x2018;Oh, I'm an actor and I'm in the Hunger Games, but I still want my character to look pretty and have good, snatched makeup,&#x2019;&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;To me, her fashion and her style isn't a vain thing. It's her form of defiance against the Capitol.&#x201D;

Below, Grace talks to Variety about playing Maysilee, details she included from Suzanne Collins&#x2019; novel and fangirling over franchise stars Jennifer Lawrence and Sam Claflin.

There's a lot. I got the braid and the bangs [from the fan film]. I know this is silly and it's not something that's mentioned in the books, but I wanted Maysilee to have different colored eyeshadows in all the scenes that we see her in. That's how she stood out as a twin and in District 12: all of her necklaces, dresses, jewelry and her braid. The Capitol is appointing them clothes. She can't have her personality shine through with her fashion, which is something she really enjoys. She has this line where she's like, &#x201C;Do we all have to look like triplets?&#x201D; because they put them in all the same clothes, and they're bland. Throughout that, she's still finding ways to stand out and be seen as a classy person. And a person, not an animal. Somebody with fashion. Somebody with personality, with dignity. So I wanted her to have that little defiance with her eyeshadow.

I also made sure that she wore a bunch of rings and jewelry. I made sure that her sleeves were torn off whenever we see her in the games, which is random. But in the books, it's mentioned that whenever they see her again, she's missing her sleeves because she ripped them off, and she has burns up her shoulders. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Also, something important to me was when Haymitch and Maysilee sit down for their picnic, I got Jo [Zada] to add back in &#x2014; because this was not in the original scene &#x2014; where he tells Maysilee about how his mom had twin girls that didn't make it. I told Jo and Francis [Lawrence, the film's director] that I felt that was so important because Maysilee, for the first time, is giving Haymitch some vulnerability. And he gives that back to her. That's so important for their relationship and such a beautiful thing for her to hear at that time. I had a lot of things that I wanted to get in there!

I don't know, because I don't think that there's any version &#x2014; I mean, of course there are ways that she's found joy, even within the games when Haymitch brings out the juice, and they sit and have their picnic. That's a moment of joy; that doesn't come with worrying about all the heaviness of the world in the games. And there are moments of connection and joy throughout it, but she's a very angry character.

I don't know if there is a version of Maysilee, even not being chosen by the games, where she feels truly happy in the world that she lives in or the circumstances that she was born into. She didn't set up that system or the world that she's in, and I don't think that she was ever truly happy in District 12, because she was just so angry at the way that it was all designed and at the games just for existing.

It was really fun. She is learning to be more outwardly kind and a little bit more sensitive to the others around her, and she's learning how to be a sister and a healer and a friend more than just being angry and lashing out at everybody throughout the film. That's kind of what her arc is. But I didn't want that arc of her learning to be kinder to diminish her anger. I didn't want it to be like, &#x201C;Oh, this angry female character all of a sudden learns how to be a sister and a mother and a friend, and she's not angry anymore and has found happiness in that.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

While she finds happiness in being kind to the people around her and protecting them, she's still a very angry character. It's really important to show young women, and anyone in general, that the two can coexist. You can be very angry at the world. You can be very loud in standing up for yourself and standing up for the people around you, but you can also be kind throughout that. That's something we lose a lot; that it has to be one or the other. But no, you can stand up; you can speak out. You don't have to box up your emotions and the things that you believe in, or make yourself more digestible for the people around you. You can still have your personality. You can still be loud about the things that you believe in, but you can still be kind and have conversations and care about people and stick up for the people around you throughout that.

It is ridiculous! It&#x2019;s insane. Jennifer Lawrence&#x2019;s comment was so funny. And the fact that Sam Claflin is commenting on my video of me dressed up [with] Finnick&#x2019;s abs painted on my shirt &#x2014; that was the funniest thing. I will never not be exposed to any celebrity that I am the biggest fan of. Between him and Josh [Hutcherson] and Jen, it&#x2019;s just ridiculous. It&#x2019;s so surreal. We&#x2019;re all such huge fans of them. Jo and I spent so many nights mulling over Josh and Jen, and I spent so long studying Sam for Finnick. It&#x2019;s such an honor that they even know who I am.

